// Title: HackTool - Htran/NATBypass Execution
// Sigma ID: f5e3b62f-e577-4e59-931e-0a15b2b94e1e
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-12-27 | Modified: 2023-02-04
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1090, S0040
// Description: Detects executable names or flags used by Htran or Htran-like tools (e.g. NATBypass)
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/HiwinCN/HTran
//   - https://github.com/cw1997/NATBypass
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_hktl_htran_or_natbypass.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\htran.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\lcx.exe") or (ProcessCommandLine contains ".exe -tran " or ProcessCommandLine contains ".exe -slave ")
